# Where witnesses work

You choose where crimes can be witnessed: only in towns, or everywhere.

## The two switches

Open `/poggy` → **Witnesses** → **Locations**.

| Only in towns | Use blacklisted areas | Result |
|---|---|---|
| On | On | Only inside enabled towns, and never inside a blacklisted area. |
| On | Off | Only inside enabled towns. |
| Off | On | Everywhere, except blacklisted areas. |
| Off | Off | Everywhere. |

A blacklisted area always wins, even where it overlaps a town.

## Adding a town

1. Stand in the middle of the town.
2. In the **Towns** list, choose **Add town**.
3. Give it a name, and use **Use my position** on **Centre**.
4. Set the **Radius** in metres. Saint Denis ships with 450 m; small
   settlements use 80 to 180 m.
5. Save and restart Witnesses.

The same town name picks the NPC lawmen for that town in
**NPC law response** → **Posse models by town**. If you add a town, you can add
a matching entry there. Without one, bounty hunters come.

## Blacklisting an area

Use **Blacklisted areas** the same way. Good places: prisons, law camps, event
areas, or anywhere a job script has lots of scripted NPCs.

## Switching an area off

Turn off **Enabled** on the row. It stays in the list for later.

## Checking a zone

Turn on **Debug output** in the **Advanced** tab (with **Show advanced** on) and restart. The zones are
drawn in the world. Turn it off again afterwards.
